# Pairs with OwnerMonotonic. The decision is not terminal-stable: an abort may
# overwrite a recorded commit, so the shards the commit's terminals have not
# reached discard their buckets and a key readers already saw committed reads
# its pre-saga value.
MODULE: OwnerMonotonicAbortOverturnsCommit
TARGET: OwnerMonotonic
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an abort overwrites a recorded commit, so a key already read committed reverts
PERTURBS: SagaAbort

--- FIND
SagaAbort ==
    /\ sg = "exec"
--- REPLACE
SagaAbort ==
\* MUTATION: an abort may overwrite a recorded decision.
    /\ sg \in {"exec", "decided"}
--- END
